  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates a hybrid classical–quantum neural network using variational circuits (up to 8 qubits and 8 layers) simulated with TensorFlow Quantum. On a credit‑scoring dataset (340–900 samples) and MNIST (1000 training images), the hybrid model achieves slightly higher metrics than a parameter‑matched classical neural network (e.g., MNIST ACC ≈0.98 train and ≈0.81 test vs ≈0.83/0.81 for the classical baseline), but all results are obtained on noiseless simulators and no scaling or complexity advantage is shown.",
